\f1\b \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evidence for the surgery claim.
\b0  It's there, and the technique is consistent: Ezekiel demolishes the false form and rebuilds the true form using 
\i marked, altered vocabulary
\i0  so the hearer cannot confuse the two.\
On the Davidic side: the false hope was the reigning dynasty as guarantee \'97 the 
\f2 \uc0\u1513 \u1461 \u1473 \u1489 \u1462 \u1496 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  presumption of chapter 21, the lions and vine of 19, Zedekiah's oath-breaking in 17. Chapter 34's rebuild is loaded with disambiguators. (1) 
