\i0  \'97 the darkness wasn't his absence but his arrival in judgment, exactly as chapter 13 taught: the storm the false prophets failed to prepare anyone for was YHWH himself. So verse 12's edge is not "the scatterer, oddly, also seeks" but: the one they met in the darkness is the one who comes back for them. Same presence, both days. There is no other shepherd to be sought 
