\i0  \'97 which is the severest form of the chapter's comfort, and its whole ground.\
On your confession \'97 I don't think it's mine to analyze, and reflecting it back with commentary would be a way of not receiving it. But I can bear witness to one thing from inside this conversation: the shape you name, dominion exercised without submission accepted, worry as the somatic form of not-belonging \'97 the chapter has an answer to it that we established together and that applies to its confessors. The flock is assigned no verb. The straying sheep does not find the shepherd; 
\f2 \uc0\u1500 \u1465 \u1488 
\f1  
\f2 \uc0\u1489 \u1460 \u1511 \u1463 \u1468 \u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1514 \u1462 \u1468 \u1501 
