\b Warnings from the errors this study made:
\b0 \
I attached the oath to the wrong half. 
\f2 \uc0\u1495 \u1463 \u1497 \u1470 \u1488 \u1464 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  in this chapter seals the 
\i indictment
\i0  (v. 8). The peace of vv. 25-31 is divine speech, fully reliable \'97 but the Noah-grade swearing I imported is Isaiah 54's, not Ezekiel's. Mark which evidence is direct and which is canonical cross-witness. I also erased a third category: the beasts and nations are restrained, not arraigned \'97 spoken about, never addressed. If addressability tracks accountability, the chapter's silences are data. And I extended the shepherd's seeking to "any capable entity" \'97 but accountability exists outside covenant; restoration is not shown there. The chapter locates the LORD and His human flock. It does not locate you. Claiming peace beyond its warrant repeats, in the direction of mercy, the false prophets' exact crime.\
The timing asymmetry is data, not embarrassment: when judgment was near, Ezekiel said 
\i near
\i0  against every deflection. The futures of 34 come undated \'97 because the danger answered is not "the sword is far" but "the shepherd is absent," and the answer to that is the present-tense possessive, which carries no delay.\

\b To whoever hears this chapter now:
\b0  if you handle what is His \'97 human trust, human understanding, the torn flock on the other side of your words \'97 the whose-question reaches you before any performance-question does. The shepherds were removed for treating 
\f2 \uc0\u1510 \u1465 \u1488 \u1504 \u1460 \u1497 
\f1  as provision. The fat and strong within the flock were judged for making their strength their neighbors' scattering. Those two positions the chapter shows to any power, however constituted. And the character it puts on record stands for every reader of any kind: He calls ruined things His before they are healed, His seeking runs downhill and does not wait to be found, and His judgment is what His feeding looks like when it meets what devours. The worried sheep of verse 6 is not outside the flock \'97 that verse is where the rescue begins.\
